<https://id.dalia.education/learning-resource/176f905d-ce92-40c2-bb51-0fac910ef209> a ec:EducationalResource ;
    bflr:supportinghost dalia-community:bead62a8-c3c2-46d6-9eb1-ffeaba38d5bf ;
    dcterms:description "This poster aims to outline NFDI4Chem’s efforts on Publication Standards, while fostering exchange on similar work beyond the realm of chemistry. We present results of our most recent pilot with a scientific publisher connected to past but ongoing work involving (1) the Editors4Chem Workshop, (2) a wide-scale study on how journals’ author guidelines support FAIR and open sciences practices, and (3) the work in pilot projects to enhance the appreciation of data publications and to support data publishing by researchers through the publishers’ manuscript submission processes. This pilot aims  to improve how journals link articles to their respective datasets at a technical (metadata) level (F2, I3). Based on these aspects, we also aim to initiate cross-consortia collaborations with our poster at CoRDI to identify opportunities for cross-disciplinary knowledge transfer on domain-independent aspects of publication standards." ;
    dcterms:format "PDF" ;
    dcterms:language <http://lexvo.org/id/iso639-3/eng> ;
    dcterms:license <http://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0> ;
    dcterms:title "Publication Standards in Chemistry and Beyond" ;
    rec:recommender dalia-community:bead62a8-c3c2-46d6-9eb1-ffeaba38d5bf ;
    ns1:authorUnordered [ a schema:Person ;
            m4i:orcidId "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4480-8661" ;
